# UI Design Conformance

This project has a single source of truth for UI/UX. Drifting from it
costs the maintainer real review time. Before writing or modifying
**any** frontend component, follow the checklist below.

## Read these first (every time)

1. [`docs/design.md`](mdc:docs/design.md) — brand colors, typography,
   spacing scale, component variants, iconography.
2. [`.cursorrules`](mdc:.cursorrules) — tech-stack mandates (shadcn/ui,
   Tremor, TanStack, lucide-react, etc.).
3. **An existing component that does something similar.** Find one
   before designing a new one. Examples that cover ~95% of UI work:
   - Audit-form questions / "pick one of N" UIs →
     [`frontend/src/utils/forms/formRendererComponents.tsx`](mdc:frontend/src/utils/forms/formRendererComponents.tsx)
     (`YesNoQuestion`, `RadioQuestion`, `MultiSelectQuestion`,
     `optionCls`).
   - Page shells / list pages →
     `frontend/src/components/common/ListPageShell.tsx`,
     `ListPageHeader.tsx`, `PageSpinner.tsx`.
   - Card / panel layout → any `<section className="rounded-xl border
     border-slate-200 bg-white">…</section>` block in
     `frontend/src/pages/quality/AIReviewerFormDetail.tsx` or
     `CalibrationMetricsPanel.tsx`.
   - Toggles → shadcn `Switch` (e.g. AIReviewerFormDetail Settings card).
   - Modals / drawers → shadcn `Dialog`, `Sheet`.

## Hard rules (non-negotiable)

- **NEVER** write a raw `<input type="radio">`, `<input
  type="checkbox">`, raw `<select>`, or hand-rolled `<button>` for
  primary actions. Use:
  - **Pick one of N (segmented)** → reuse the `optionCls` pill
    pattern from `formRendererComponents.tsx`. This is the canonical
    QTIP "radio" style.
  - **Boolean toggle** → shadcn `Switch`.
  - **Dropdown** → shadcn `Select`.
  - **Primary / secondary / destructive button** → shadcn `Button`
    with the standard variants. Primary buttons are
    `bg-primary hover:bg-primary/90 text-white`.
  - **Form input** → shadcn `Input`, `Label`, `textarea` from
    `components/ui/textarea`.
- **NEVER** introduce a new color outside the QTIP brand palette
  defined in `docs/design.md` and `.cursorrules`. The palette is
  exposed as Tailwind tokens (`bg-primary`, `text-primary`, `bg-success`,
  `bg-warning`, `bg-destructive`, `bg-surface`, `text-neutral-700`,
  `text-neutral-900`). Hex values like `#00aeef` are only acceptable
  when copying an exact existing utility class (e.g.
  `border-[#00aeef]` from `optionCls`).
- **NEVER** build a custom data table — use TanStack Table.
- **NEVER** use `useEffect` + `axios`/`fetch` for server state — use
  TanStack Query.
- **NEVER** introduce another icon library or emojis — only
  `lucide-react`.
- **NEVER** add custom CSS files. Tailwind utilities only.
- **NEVER** invent a new spacing scale. Stick to the 8-pt scale
  documented in `docs/design.md` (2, 4, 8, 12, 16, 24, 32…).

## Workflow before any new UI

```
1. Read docs/design.md  (or skim if read this session)
2. Grep for the closest existing component:
     - Is there already a YES_NO-style picker? → reuse optionCls.
     - Is there already a list page? → reuse ListPageShell.
     - Is there already a settings card? → copy AIReviewerFormDetail's pattern.
3. If a shadcn primitive doesn't exist yet, ASK the user before
   adding @radix-ui/* packages. Do not silently expand the
   dependency tree.
4. Only then write the component, mirroring the closest existing
   one's class names, spacing, and structure.
```

## When in doubt

Stop. Show the user the existing component you plan to mimic and
confirm before writing the new one. It is always cheaper than
re-doing the design afterward.
